{"name":"Yacht Harbour","hex":"#7c9dae","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"yacht","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A slick and light ship for making pleasure trips or racing on water, having sails but often motor-powered. At times used as a residence offshore on a dock.","Any vessel used for private, noncommercial purposes."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To sail, voyage, or race in a yacht."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yacht"},{"term":"harbour","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Standard spelling of harbor."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Standard spelling of harbor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harbour"}],"entries":[{"title":"Marina","blocks":[{"text":"A marina is a dock or area of water with piers and moorings for securing and parking yachts and small boats. A marina differs from a port in that a marina is not designed to handle large passenger ships or freighters, and is often for leisure boating activities such as yachting, sailing and boat tours."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Guarda-corpo_da_Avenida_Portugal_-_Rio_de_Janeiro_-_20220923024517.jpg/330px-Guarda-corpo_da_Avenida_Portugal_-_Rio_de_Janeiro_-_20220923024517.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marina"},{"title":"Yacht","blocks":[{"text":"A yacht is a sail- or motor-propelled watercraft made for pleasure, cruising, or racing. There is no standard definition, though the term generally applies to vessels with a cabin intended for overnight use."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Bavaria_Cruiser_45.jpg/330px-Bavaria_Cruiser_45.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yacht"},{"title":"Harbor","blocks":[{"text":"A harbor or harbour is a sheltered part of a body of water where ships, boats, and barges c